  "shortName": null,
  "description": "Camp Tiny Paws, originally Tiny Paws Con, was a furry convention held in Danbury, Connecticut. It was started in 2017 by K'gra Leopard, a founder and co-chair of FurFright, and Nobody, a former assistant dealer director. The convention offered a dealers' room, tabletop gaming, charity tables and programming focused on creative activities, and it supported the Connecticut Humane Society. After three editions at the Crowne Plaza Danbury, it was held online in 2021 as Camp Pannycake and was succeeded by an online event, the Weekend Furry Retreat.",
